Plumb Developer Dashboard (Frontend)

Welcome to the frontend repository of Plumb, a lightweight Domain-Specific Language (DSL) designed for describing simple data pipelines with visual compiler diagnostics and real-time telemetry.

This React-based web dashboard (built with Vite and styled with Tailwind CSS) allows developers to write Plumb code, compile it via the backend API, inspect the AST (Abstract Syntax Tree), view token distribution analytics, and examine generated JavaScript code in a clean, professional, developer-first interface.

🖥️ Frontend Architecture, Screens & Components

The dashboard is structured as a single-page application with a tabbed navigation architecture. Below is the comprehensive breakdown of all screens, modular components, and their specific interactive features.

1. Navigation & Global Layout

Header / Top Navigation Bar (Header.jsx)

App Title & Subtitle: Displays "Plumb" alongside "Developer Dashboard".

Live Connection Status: Features a live pulsing green badge reading "Backend connected" (clickable/hoverable to display connection latency or endpoint status).

Navigation Tabs (NavigationTabs.jsx): Allows seamless switching between primary views:

Compiler (Active default view)

AST Viewer

Metrics

Settings

2. Screen 1: The Compiler Dashboard (CompilerScreen.jsx)

This is the primary workspace where developers write and compile their .plb pipeline code and review immediate telemetry and compilation outputs. It is split into distinct functional panels:

A. Code Editor Panel (CodeEditor.jsx)

Header: Displays file identifier (main.plb).

Text Area / Editor: Line-numbered text editor pre-loaded with boilerplate Plumb code:

pipeline process_data
    read "users.csv"
    filter age > 18
    transform name
    output "result.csv"


Action Buttons:

Compile Button (CompileButton.jsx): Primary indigo-filled button with hover states. Dispatches the code to the backend API.

Clear Button (ClearButton.jsx): Secondary outline button to reset the code editor input.

B. Compilation Metrics Panel (MetricsPanel.jsx)

A grid of 6 interactive metric cards displaying real-time telemetry upon compilation:

Compile time: e.g., 24 ms

Tokens: e.g., 12

AST nodes: e.g., 9

Errors: e.g., 0

Warnings: e.g., 0

Status: Success (Green status badge)

C. Token Distribution Breakdown (TokenDistribution.jsx)

Interactive horizontal progress bars and percentage distributions categorized by token types:

Keywords: 5 (41.7%)

Identifiers: 3 (25.0%)

Strings: 2 (16.7%)

Operators: 1 (8.3%)

Numbers: 1 (8.3%)

D. AST Viewer Panel (ASTViewer.jsx)

Expandable/collapsible hierarchical tree view representing the parsed syntax tree nodes:

Pipeline: process_data
├── Read
│   └── "users.csv"
├── Filter
│   └── age > 18
├── Transform
│   └── name
└── Output
    └── "result.csv"


E. Diagnostics Panel (DiagnosticsPanel.jsx)

Success summary container (✓ Compilation successful) or detailed error cards showing line numbers, column numbers, explanations, and autocomplete suggestions (e.g., "Did you mean 'filter'?").

F. Generated Code Panel (GeneratedCode.jsx)

Displays the target language tag (Target: JavaScript).

Code display block showing the transpiled JavaScript output (readCSV, .filter(), .map(), writeCSV) with a quick-copy icon button.

3. Screen 2: Dedicated AST Viewer Tab (ASTTabScreen.jsx)

Provides an expanded, full-screen interactive view of the Abstract Syntax Tree.

Allows zooming, node collapsing/expanding, and inspection of node metadata (such as node type, child count, and token spans).

4. Screen 3: Metrics & Telemetry Tab (MetricsTabScreen.jsx)

Deep-dive analytics screen showing historical compilation performance metrics.

Visual charts tracking compilation duration trends over multiple runs and comprehensive token type distribution graphs.

5. Screen 4: Settings Tab (SettingsScreen.jsx)

Configuration panel for developer preferences.

Options include toggling dark/light theme, configuring custom Backend API base URLs (VITE_API_BASE_URL), and adjusting compiler strictness flags.

