⚙️ Getting Started & Installation

Follow these steps to run the Vite frontend development server locally:

Prerequisites

Node.js (v18+ recommended)

npm, yarn, or pnpm

1. Clone the Repository

git clone https://github.com/your-username/plumb.git
cd plumb/frontend


2. Install Dependencies

npm install


3. Configure Environment Variables

Create a .env file in the root of the frontend directory. Vite requires environment variables to use the VITE_ prefix:

VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000/api


4. Run the Development Server

Start the Vite development server with HMR:

npm run dev


Open the provided local URL (typically http://localhost:5173) in your browser.

5. Build for Production

To generate an optimized production build:

npm run build


🔌 Backend API Integration Contract

The frontend posts user-authored Plumb scripts to the backend API:

Endpoint: POST /api/compile

Request Payload (JSON):

{
  "code": "pipeline process_data\n    read \"users.csv\"\n    filter age > 18\n    output \"result.csv\""
}


Response Payload (JSON):

{
  "status": "success",
  "compilationTime": 24,
  "tokenCount": 12,
  "astNodes": 9,
  "errors": 0,
  "warnings": 0,
  "astTree": { ... },
  "generatedCode": "const data = readCSV(\"users.csv\");\nconst filtered = data.filter(r => r.age > 18);\nwriteCSV(filtered, \"result.csv\");"
}